    17	Defined in `backend/app/models.py` as `class User(UserBase, table=True)`.
    18	
    19	# Schema
    20	
    21	| Column | Type | Notes |
    22	|---|---|---|
    23	| `id` | UUID | Primary key, `default_factory=uuid.uuid4` |
    24	| `email` | string, ≤255 | Unique, indexed |
    25	| `hashed_password` | string | Argon2 (or legacy bcrypt) hash. Never returned by the API. |
    26	| `is_active` | bool | Default `true`. Inactive users are rejected at login and by `get_current_user`. |
    27	| `is_superuser` | bool | Default `false`. Gates admin-only routes via `get_current_active_superuser`. |
    28	| `full_name` | string \| null, ≤255 | Optional |
    29	| `created_at` | datetime (tz-aware) | `default_factory` set at insert time |
    30	
    31	# Relationships
    32	
    33	- `items: list[Item]` — back-populates `Item.owner`, `cascade_delete=True` (deleting a
    34	  user deletes their items at the ORM level; the FK also has `ondelete="CASCADE"` at the
    35	  DB level, see [item](item.md)).
    36	
    37	# API-facing variants (all in `models.py`)
    38	
    39	- `UserCreate` — used by admin-only `POST /users/`, includes `password`.
    40	- `UserRegister` — used by public `POST /users/signup`, includes `password`, excludes
    41	  `is_active`/`is_superuser` (self-signup can't grant yourself admin).
    42	- `UserUpdate` / `UserUpdateMe` — admin update vs. self-service update (the latter can't
    43	  change `is_active`/`is_superuser`).
    44	- `UpdatePassword` — `current_password` + `new_password`, for `PATCH /users/me/password`.
    45	- `UserPublic` — the only shape ever returned by the API; omits `hashed_password`.
    46	
    47	See [routers/users](../routers/users.md) for the endpoints that operate on this table.

